[b]Disclaimer: the code of this script was written 100% by Claude Opus 5.5 (an AI by Anthropic). It was tested in game by me.[/b]

[h1]Dock Gate - companion for Acceleration Control[/h1]
Put this script on your [b]base[/b]. When a ship running [i]Acceleration Control[/i] (link below) docks or undocks, it asks the base over the antenna to open the way in; this script triggers your timer blocks and tells the ship when the gate is open.

[h2]Setup[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Load the script into a programmable block on the base. Base and ship need antennas in range (relays work).
[*]Build a timer block named [b]Dock Open[/b] whose toolbar opens the way in (hangar doors, pistons, rotors, lights - anything), and one named [b]Dock Close[/b] that closes it.
[*]Optional: name the moving parts [b]Dock Gate[/b] or put them in a group of that name. The base then reports "ready" only when all of them have stopped (doors open, pistons and rotors at rest).
[*]Dock by hand once with the ship, so it knows which connector to ask for.
[/olist]

[h2]Several docks on one base[/h2]
Add a part of the connector's name: timers [i]Dock Open Hangar A[/i] / [i]Dock Close Hangar A[/i] and group [i]Dock Gate Hangar A[/i] belong to the connector [i]Connector Hangar A[/i]. Names without such a part belong to every connector - then the gate also opens when a ship docks at another connector.

Run the block with [i]open[/i] or [i]close[/i] to test the timers by hand.

